## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an extensible editor action system with undo/redo using a runtime registry and the Command pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Command pattern for reversible actions
- Runtime extensibility via a simple registry
- Text buffer abstraction and range handling
- Undo/redo stack semantics

## Code Example
```javascript
class TextBuffer {
  constructor(text){ this.text = text }
  replace(start, end, replacement){
    this.text = this.text.slice(0, start) + replacement + this.text.slice(end)
  }
}
class Command {
  constructor(ctx, range){ this.ctx = ctx; this.range = range }
  execute(){ }
  undo(){ }
}
class Registry {
  constructor(){ this.factories = new Map() }
  register(name, factory){ this.factories.set(name, factory) }
  create(name, ctx, range){ const f = this.factories.get(name); return f ? f(ctx, range) : null }
}
class UppercaseCommand extends Command {
  execute(){ const s = this.ctx.buffer.text.substring(this.range.start, this.range.end); this.prev = s; this.ctx.buffer.replace(this.range.start, this.range.end, s.toUpperCase()) }
  undo(){ this.ctx.buffer.replace(this.range.start, this.range.end, this.prev) }
}
```

